  "name": "Wickermoor, the night before",
  "region": "wickers_vigil",
  "summary": "The Founder's Round on the eve of the burning: carts across the moor road, a long table under lanterns, a bonfire on the hill, a goat on the notice board.",
  "text": "The bonfire on the hill north of the village is visible from every window, and the village has gone out to meet it: carts and planks barring the moor road, volunteers lining up in a queue that bends round the well, a long table under lanterns, and across the way the stone door of the Silent Church standing open. The goat is on the notice board.",
